/*  The project of Cufet written in Cufet — and the first to draw its tree.

    ★★ `Cufet` is ONE namespace over its folders. What they share — `node`, `token`, the
    scanner, the words for types — sits in `Cufet/` itself, which each folder sees by plain
    name. Each folder keeps its own names besides, so `lexer/`, `parser/` and `checker/` may each
    have a `counted`; one reaches another's by qualifying it, as the checker does with
    `parser's program-tree`.

    ⚠ Once a project draws its tree it draws every folder with Cufet source in it. A new folder
    here needs a line before anything in it can be checked.
*/

Pull a book on blueprints.
    Bind text to tree:
        Return <<
Cufet
    lexer
    parser
    checker
    compiler
>>.
    Done.
Done.
